  "scope": "Three public requests at seed 8102. Roof-on exterior, sampled functional room groups and secondary cutaway. This is comparison evidence, not the full house-style acceptance matrix.",
  "findings": [
    "Terracotta roof and teal shutters provide some identity, but the exterior is a plain rectangle with little shaded arrival, veranda or garden relation.",
    "The interior keeps generic cottage furniture and plank floors; it lacks the plaster/stone, shade and fitted household arrangements in the target.",
    "The default parlour is a bench in a long bare room. The small arrival camera faces an empty entrance wall; it is only one eye view and does not establish that the whole hall is empty.",
    "Kitchen prep stations and wall storage are isolated objects rather than a fitted cooking corner.",
    "The large cutaway repeats sparse rooms around an empty corridor. The large exterior has a blank side wall and a tiny entrance.",
    "Bedrooms and stores repeat generic bed/chest and barrel/crate layouts without a coherent style-specific material or use arrangement."
  ],
